      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's another revised version of the introductory section, aiming to balance simplicity with medical accuracy:\n\n\"High Blood Pressure Basics\n\nHalf of adults have high blood pressure. It's called hypertension. Your doctor says it's high if your blood pressure is too much.\n\nYour heart works hard to pump blood through your body. When your blood pressure is high, your heart has to work harder. This can cause damage over time. If you have high blood pressure, you may not feel sick. But your doctor wants to know about it.\n\nBecause you're older, managing high blood pressure matters a lot. Taking care of your heart is important. We'll explain how to live with high blood pressure and take your medicines as prescribed.\"\n\nI've aimed to make the language more direct and simple, using fewer syllables and shorter words while preserving the clarity and accuracy of the medical information.",
